      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e We can probably squeeze a bit more performance if dst, above and left can be guaranteed to be aligned at 32 byte (AVX2) or 64 byte (AVX512) boundary, but I don\u0027t have enough context to make such a change.\n\u003e \n\u003e No, that won\u0027t be possible given the partitioning and use of other intra predictor sizes.\n\nNot for all sizes. I suspect that currently we allocate a full frame on a 16-byte boundary currently, which allows us to use aligned SSE access on 8x8 and larger sizes. If we can start the full frame from a 64 byte boundary, we can use aligned AVX access on 16x16 and larger, and aligned AVX512 access on 32x32.",
